{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Da5duqBUMxArgRakmzjrVA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t \"number\": 27,\n3\t \"title\": \"Linux: webContents.print() returns \\\"Invalid printer settings\\\" in Electron 43, works in Electron 42\",\n4\t \"body\": \"### Preflight Checklist\\n\\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a bug report that matches the one I want to file, without success.\\n\\n### Electron Version\\n\\n43.0.0\\n\\n### What operating system(s) are you using?\\n\\nUbuntu\\n\\n### Operating System Version\\n\\nUbuntu 24.06 (x11)\\n\\n### What arch are you using?\\n\\nx64\\n\\n### Last Known Working Electron version\\n\\n42.6.0\\n\\n### Does the issue also appear in Chromium / Google Chrome?\\n\\nNo\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n`win.webContents.print` with a non empty options object (for example, `{silent: true, deviceName: \\\"MyPrinter\\\"}`) is supposed to print the content seamlessly.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\n`win.webContents.print` with an empty options (`{}`) object, opens the print dialog alright but when I put options like `silent` or `deviceName` the function throws `Invalid printer settings`.\\n\\n### Testcase Gist URL\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\n_No response_\",\n5\t \"labels\": [\n6\t  \"43-x-y\",\n7\t  \"bug :beetle:\",\n8\t  \"platform/linux\"\n9\t ],\n10\t \"state\": \"open\",\n11\t \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n12\t \"as_of\": \"2026-07-06T13:58:01Z\",\n13\t \"replay\": true\n14\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b16ac663-8126-4795-9747-72f9d1465ada","uuid":"8a51afca-2958-4df7-9e58-6bb0bf9a0d70","timestamp":"2026-10-